(4,'ed2df575d4b9',7,'Ethics and professionalism','A patient with decision-making capacity refuses a recommended treatment after understanding the risks. Which principle supports respecting that decision?','Autonomy',['Paternalism','Commercial interest','Professional convenience'],'Autonomy supports an informed, voluntary choice by a patient with decision-making capacity.'),
(4,'ed2df575d4b9',7,'Ethics and professionalism','Which principle supports fair allocation of limited healthcare resources?','Justice',['Personal preference','Financial profit','Paternalism'],'Justice requires fair allocation according to relevant clinical needs rather than irrelevant personal characteristics.'),
(4,'ed2df575d4b9',15,'Ethics and professionalism','What is an error of omission?','Failing to perform a necessary action',['Performing an unnecessary procedure','Giving the wrong medicine','Using the wrong dose'],'An omission is failure to take an indicated action; commission involves performing an incorrect action.'),
