(3,'351e54a569c0',2,'Laboratory interpretation','Which laboratory pattern is typical of vitamin B12 deficiency?','Increased methylmalonic acid and homocysteine',['Normal methylmalonic acid and homocysteine','Increased homocysteine with normal methylmalonic acid','Decreased methylmalonic acid and homocysteine'],'Vitamin B12 is required for metabolism of both methylmalonic acid and homocysteine. Folate deficiency generally raises homocysteine without raising methylmalonic acid.'),
